' World-space (x/z, no y - guards stay on the ground plane) point a GuardPlacement's
' `patrolTo` targets.
interface GuardPatrolTarget
  x as float
  z as float
end interface

' A single Guard placement consumed by WorldRoom.addGuards(). `patrolTo`/`patrolSpeed`
' are only meaningful (and only ever set) together - invalid `patrolTo` means stand idle
' instead of patrolling (see Guard.bs).
interface GuardPlacement
  x as float
  z as float
  rotY as float
  patrolTo as GuardPatrolTarget
  patrolSpeed as float
end interface

' Fixed placements for Guard entities in WorldRoom (issue #104). Coordinates are
' measured directly off worldMap.png's own pixel content (1:1 with world x/z, see
' WorldRoom.bs's mapOverlay setup) so both guards land on real ground features rather
' than arbitrary points:
' - The first Guard patrols back and forth across the wooden bridge spanning the
'   lake's northeast inlet, playing its walk animation and facing the direction of
'   travel (see Guard.bs).
' - The second Guard just stands (idle) on the dirt stepping-stone path north of the
'   lake.
function getGuardPlacements() as GuardPlacement[]
  return [
    {x: 190.0, z: -255.0, rotY: 0.0, patrolTo: {x: 290.0, z: -147.0}, patrolSpeed: 15.0}
    {x: -195.0, z: -380.0, rotY: 90.0}
  ]
end function
